S2 classification spike

No third-party word lists or classifier implementation code were copied.
The short baseline patterns and invented corpus are original to this spike.

Runtime dependencies are retained by the standalone lockfile:
- @huggingface/transformers 4.3.0, Apache-2.0
- @mlc-ai/web-llm 0.2.85, Apache-2.0
- onnxruntime-web 1.31.0-dev.20260914-8d85527a0, MIT
- playwright 1.63.0, Apache-2.0
- vite 7.3.7, MIT
- linked @socialprune/core is first-party SocialPrune code; its runtime
  dependencies are zod 4.6.5 (MIT) and @zip.js/zip.js 2.23.0 (BSD-3-Clause).

The license audit reads all reachable installed package manifests and the linked
core's runtime dependencies. Exact transitive versions remain in pnpm-lock.yaml.
Upstream license files remain with their packages. No downloaded model, browser
binary or WASM library is part of the source delivery.

Model licenses are separate from the code audit:
- Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B and Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B, Apache-2.0, upstream Qwen team.
  Ollama's qwen3:0.6b and qwen3:1.7b /api/show license text says Apache 2.0.
  The mlc-ai conversions name these base models but do not repeat a license
  field; the upstream model license is the provenance used in this trial.
- MoritzLaurer/mDeBERTa-v3-base-xnli-multilingual-nli-2mil7, MIT, Moritz Laurer.
  The original repository supplies the tested ONNX conversion itself.
- Gemini Nano would be supplied under Chrome's model distribution terms, not
  under this spike's code license; no Gemini model was downloaded here.

Prebuilt Qwen model libraries were downloaded for local execution from
mlc-ai/binary-mlc-llm-libs commit
025bcaf3780fa8254f5e5efd3bfea0a5397248f4, web-llm-models/v0_2_84/base.
MLC LLM and WebLLM source are Apache-2.0, but S3 found no standalone license
in that binary repository. Redistribution permission remains unestablished;
these generated, ignored binaries must not be distributed with the product
until that provenance question is resolved.

